OL,3,GNEWSAFilm shares 'rich tapestry' of
OL,4,AWindrush children's lives
OL,5,
OL,6,FFilm co-producer and project curator
OL,7,FRoger Griffith MBE said he wanted to
OL,8,Fchampion those pioneering parents,
OL,9,Fwhile sharing how their children grew
OL,10,Fup in the "rich tapestry" of a
OL,11,FBristolian, British, black experience
OL,12,Fwhile overcoming "racism, institutional
OL,13,Fdiscrimination and a clash of
OL,14,Fcultures".
OL,16,FBroadcaster Sherrie Eugene-Hart shares
OL,17,Fher story and said she hoped people
OL,18,Fwere left with a sense of pride, hope
OL,19,Fand achievement.
